<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>ZEN DLNA Server</title>
    @* The server's own device icon, served on the admin port so no admin page names the media port. *@
    <link rel="icon" href="/admin/favicon.ico" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/DlnaServer.Admin/admin.css" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
    @* Static by default, interactive per page. Making the whole router interactive opened a
       SignalR circuit for every page - and a circuit owns a DI scope holding a DlnaDbContext and
       therefore a pooled SQLite connection with its own page cache. The Dashboard is the landing page
       and the one most likely left open in a tab, and it has no buttons at all: it now costs a render
       and nothing else. Every page that does have controls opts in with @@rendermode InteractiveServer,
       and a page that forgets to loses its buttons visibly rather than silently. *@
    <Routes />
    <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
